# The public upterm relay's host key, as an SSH certificate authority.
#
# uptermd presents a host certificate, signed with its own key.
# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/knownhosts only treats a key as a host authority when
# its line is marked @cert-authority, and upterm 0.37.0 and earlier accept the
# certificate no other way: the plain key line an `ssh-keyscan` of this relay
# emits never matches, and they fall through to the first-connection prompt.
# Later releases also check the certificate's own key against plain lines, as
# OpenSSH does.
#
# Both lines are needed because a known_hosts pattern matches the port exactly:
# a bare host means port 22, and a wss:// connection is keyed as [host]:443.
#
# Verify against the fingerprint published in the README before trusting this
# file.
@cert-authority uptermd.upterm.dev ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAICiecex8Dq718eSe1CCLgLvDmI7AagvCtax7brPFWkh4
@cert-authority [uptermd.upterm.dev]:443 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAICiecex8Dq718eSe1CCLgLvDmI7AagvCtax7brPFWkh4
